Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 08:51:41 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 330/333] [ae-patch] Read a chat's running Claude login before
 its stored pick, and say when a switch waits for the next message

A switch on a chat with no running terminal stores the new login for its next
start, so the stored pick and the running login differ until then. The web read
the stored pick first while the server reads the running login first, so the
Switch account button offered the login the chat already ran on, and each tap
flipped the stored pick back and forth without restarting anything.

aeChatAccount now reads the running login first, as the server does. The menu
sends a switch unless the login is both running and stored, so picking the
running login puts it back as the stored one. A switch the server answers with
queued (no terminal running) toasts "This chat starts on X at its next
message" instead of "now runs on X".
